Here's the structured goal model based on the mission description:

### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|--------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1     | Complete Collection-Delivery Mission | Ensure resources are collected and delivered successfully. | ; | Achieve | - |
| G2     | Complete Collection Phase | Collect required resources from storage. | ; | Achieve | G1 |
| G3     | Complete Delivery Phase | Deliver collected resources to the specified location. | ; | Achieve | G1 |
| G21    | Navigate to Storage | Move to the storage location. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G22    | Request Resources | Send a message to the storage for resources. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G23    | Ensure Battery Level >10% | Maintain battery level above 10%. | FALLBACK(G23_success, G23_failure) | Achieve | G2 |
| G31    | Navigate to Delivery Location | Move to the delivery point. | - | Perform | G3 |
| G32    | Deliver Resources | Transfer resources to the specified location. | - | Perform | G3 |
| G33    | Ensure Battery Level >30% | Maintain battery level above 30%. | FALLBACK(G33_success, G33_failure) | Achieve | G3 |

### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|------------------|
| AT21    | Navigate to Storage | Move to the storage area. | AND | Storage | 1 |
| AT22    | Request Resources | Send resource request to storage. | AND | Storage | 1 |
| AT23    | Recharge Battery | Return to recharge station. | AND | Recharge Station | 1 |
| AT24    | Assign Mission | Transfer mission to another robot. | AND | Current Location | 1 |
| AT31    | Navigate to Delivery Point | Move to delivery location. | AND | Delivery Location | 1 |
| AT32    | Deliver Resources | Transfer resources to destination. | AND | Delivery Location | 1 |
| AT33    | Return to Checkpoint | Bring resources back to checkpoint. | AND | Checkpoint | 1 |
| AT34    | Assign Remaining Task | Transfer remaining task to another robot. | AND | Checkpoint | 1 |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3** [AND] (Sequential execution)
- **G2 -> G21, G22, G23** [AND] (Sequential execution)
- **G3 -> G31, G32, G33** [AND] (Sequential execution)
- **G23 -> AT23, AT24** [AND] (Sequential execution)
- **G33 -> AT33, AT34** [AND] (Sequential execution)

This model ensures that the mission is decomposed into manageable goals and tasks, with appropriate fallback mechanisms for battery management.
